-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1000: an export overrides a section GIVEN with an inner
-- WITH. `inner` reads `r`; the second read of it is pinned to 100 for that
-- call only, so the first read sees the row's value (or the default).
-- `l4 run` answers 103; `l4 batch` used to refuse the module with
-- "You are giving named inputs to inner ... of type NUMBER".

§ `Rates`
    GIVEN r IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3

GIVETH A NUMBER
inner MEANS r

@export One read takes the rate, one overrides it
GIVEN b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
outer b MEANS b PLUS inner PLUS (inner WITH r IS 100)

#EVAL outer 0
